# Deny-by-default, then allow exactly what the image needs.
#
# This is inverted from the usual "list the junk" style on purpose. A denylist
# fails open: every new secret, cache dir, or dump file added to the repo is
# silently shipped into the build context until someone remembers to add a line.
# An allowlist fails closed - `.env`, `.env.*`, `var/`, `logs/`, and anything
# else added tomorrow cannot leak into the context or into an image layer.
#
# Keep in sync with the COPY instructions in Dockerfile.
*

# --- dependency manifests (builder stage) ---
!pyproject.toml
!poetry.lock
# `poetry check --lock` validates the whole manifest, including that the declared
# readme exists - so README.md must be in the context for the lockfile gate to run.
!README.md

# --- application + migrations (runtime stage) ---
!app/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini

# --- re-exclude build noise that lives inside the allowed directories ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
